<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21192] OST objects that are never written have no parent FID</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21192</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;An OST object records the FID of the file it belongs to (its parent FID, in trusted.fid) only when a client sends it with a write, punch, fallocate or setattr. An object that is never written never gets one: the objects of empty files, of instantiated PFL components past the end of a file, and of files created and never written.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Such objects cannot be mapped back to their file:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lfs fid2path of the OST object FID fails, which matters for objects found corrupted, or removed by e2fsck.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;A tool that reads an OST to find the files on it, such as lfs drain (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20908" title="Standalone multithreaded utility for parallel OST migration" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20908"&gt;LU-20908&lt;/a&gt;), cannot tell these objects from precreated ones, and has to walk the whole namespace to find their files, which is expensive.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Layout LFSCK takes an object with no parent FID as consistent and leaves it so (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-11628" title="LFSCK doesn't recover missing PFID" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-11628"&gt;LU-11628&lt;/a&gt;; its patch, change 33591, was abandoned).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;The OSS cannot fix this on its own: no RPC that reaches an unwritten object carries the parent FID (a read of an empty file is answered from the glimpse, and OST_GETATTR carries none), and the resource ID repair of &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18756" title="tag all OST objects with parent FID" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18756"&gt;LU-18756&lt;/a&gt; skips objects that were never written. Only the MDT knows the owner.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix, in two patches:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;This ticket, Gerrit change 70746 (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21192" title="OST objects that are never written have no parent FID" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-21192"&gt;LU-21192&lt;/a&gt; osp: send the parent FID of new OST objects): when LOD creates the objects of a layout, it passes the parent FID and stripe index to OSP, which queues a setattr record per object in its sync llog, in the create transaction. The sync thread sends it as an OST_SETATTR with OBD_MD_FLFID, as it already does for ownership changes, so creates do not wait for it. The parent FID goes in the padding of llog_setattr64_rec_v2. The OST stores it only if the object has none, since a record can arrive after a layout swap has given the object another parent. osp.*.create_pfid=0 turns it off.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-11628" title="LFSCK doesn't recover missing PFID" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-11628"&gt;LU-11628&lt;/a&gt;, Gerrit change 70747 (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-11628" title="LFSCK doesn't recover missing PFID" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-11628"&gt;LU-11628&lt;/a&gt; lfsck: give OST objects a missing parent FID): layout LFSCK gives an object with no parent FID the FID, stripe index and owner of the MDT-object that references it, as for an unmatched pair, so files created before 70746 are fixed too.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;lfs drain (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20908" title="Standalone multithreaded utility for parallel OST migration" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20908"&gt;LU-20908&lt;/a&gt;, changes 70470 and 70471) is rebased on both and no longer walks the namespace.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Objects precreated and not yet used (at or above the MDT's prealloc_next_id) need no parent FID.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
